      "writtenOn": "2016-06-01T06:54:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are right, this mocks time outside of monasca_common.kafka.producer. In unit tests I usually try to mock everything that is outside of the module being tested. That way I can be sure that no \"real\" functions (outside of the module) are called so I think this mock would not mess up other modules.\n\nBut I get your point. In a less controlled environment this could cause trouble.\n\nI can change it back, but I prefer not to change (mock) any part of the module that is being tested, unless there is no other way, like in the case of monasca_common.kafka.producer.log.",
